     5→title: CLI Interface
     6→type: module
     7→status:
     8→  maturity: draft
     9→  implementation: not_started
    10→description: |
    11→  The kspec CLI is the primary interface to Kynetic Spec.
    12→  Follows git's plumbing/porcelain model: low-level primitives
    13→  for scripts/agents, high-level commands for humans.
    14→features:
    15→  - _ulid: 01KEZCJPHW3CSMXYZT01FP76BM
    16→    slugs:
    17→      - cli-design
    18→    title: CLI Design Principles
    19→    type: feature
    20→    status:
    21→      maturity: draft
    22→      implementation: not_started
    23→    priority: high
    24→    tags:
    25→      - mvp
    26→      - cli
    27→    description: |
    28→      The CLI is designed for both human and agent use.
    29→      Consistent structure, predictable output, clear errors.
    30→    requirements:
    31→      - _ulid: 01KEZCJPHWP32HK8MR38P2WSSJ
    32→        slugs:
    33→          - cli-structure
    34→        title: Command Structure
    35→        type: requirement
    36→        status:
    37→          maturity: draft
    38→          implementation: not_started
    39→        description: |
    40→          Commands follow consistent structure:
    41→
    42→          kspec <resource> <action> [args] [flags]
    43→
    44→          Resources: item, task, link, todo, etc.
    45→          Actions: add, get, list, set, delete, etc.
    46→
    47→          Examples:
    48→          - kspec item add --type feature --title "Login"
    49→          - kspec task start @impl-login
    50→          - kspec tasks ready
    51→        implements:
    52→          - '@cli-design'
    53→      - _ulid: 01KEZCJPHWKVBFSAEP0MMH57DQ
    54→        slugs:
