   343→      - _ulid: 01KF3E3QPARGX5QWJMT231DCC5
   344→        slugs:
   345→          - item-patch
   346→        title: kspec item patch
   347→        type: requirement
   348→        tags:
   349→          - cli
   350→          - dx
   351→        depends_on: []
   352→        implements: []
   353→        relates_to: []
   354→        tests: []
   355→        created: '2026-01-16T12:57:30.058Z'
   356→        description: |-
   357→          kspec item patch <ref> [options]
   358→
   359→          Update spec item with JSON data.
   360→
   361→          Options:
   362→          - --data <json>: JSON object with fields to update
   363→          - --bulk: Read multiple patches from stdin (JSONL or JSON array)
   364→          - --fail-fast: Stop on first error in bulk mode (default: continue)
   365→          - --dry-run: Show what would change without writing
   366→          - --allow-unknown: Allow unknown fields (for extending format)
   367→
   368→          Single item mode:
   369→            kspec item patch @my-item --data '{"title": "New"}'
   370→            echo '{"title": "New"}' | kspec item patch @my-item
   371→
   372→          Bulk mode (JSONL or JSON array on stdin):
   373→            cat patches.jsonl | kspec item patch --bulk
   374→            echo '[{"ref":"@a","data":{...}}]' | kspec item patch --bulk
   375→
   376→          Validates input against SpecItemInputSchema (strict by default).
   377→        acceptance_criteria:
   378→          - id: ac-1
   379→            given: valid JSON with status field
   380→            when: kspec item patch @my-item --data '{"status":{"implementation":"implemented"}}' runs
   381→            then: item status is updated to implemented
   382→          - id: ac-2
   383→            given: invalid JSON syntax
   384→            when: kspec item patch @my-item --data 'not json' runs
   385→            then: error with helpful JSON parse message
   386→          - id: ac-3
   387→            given: JSON piped via stdin
   388→            when: echo '{"title":"New"}' | kspec item patch @my-item runs
   389→            then: stdin JSON is used for update
   390→          - id: ac-4
   391→            given: '--dry-run flag provided'
   392→            when: kspec item patch @my-item --data '{"title":"New"}' --dry-run runs
   393→            then: shows what would change without writing
   394→          - id: ac-5
   395→            given: JSON with unknown field 'foobar'
   396→            when: kspec item patch @my-item --data '{"foobar":"value"}' runs
   397→            then: error about unknown field
   398→          - id: ac-6
   399→            given: JSON with unknown field and --allow-unknown flag
   400→            when: kspec item patch @my-item --data '{"foobar":"value"}' --allow-unknown runs
   401→            then: field is written to item
   402→          - id: ac-7
   403→            given: JSONL with multiple patches on stdin
   404→            when: cat patches.jsonl | kspec item patch --bulk runs
   405→            then: all items updated, summary shown
   406→          - id: ac-8
   407→            given: JSON array with multiple patches on stdin
   408→            when: echo '[{"ref":"@a","data":{...}}]' | kspec item patch --bulk runs
   409→            then: all items updated, summary shown
   410→          - id: ac-9
   411→            given: bulk mode with one invalid ref among valid
   412→            when: command runs without --fail-fast
   413→            then: valid items updated, errors reported, exit 1
   414→          - id: ac-10
   415→            given: bulk mode with --fail-fast and first ref invalid
   416→            when: command runs
   417→            then: stops immediately, no items updated, exit 1
   418→          - id: ac-11
   419→            given: ref points to a task (not spec item)
   420→            when: kspec item patch @some-task --data '{...}' runs
   421→            then: 'error: Not a spec item'
   422→          - id: ac-12
   423→            given: ref does not exist
   424→            when: kspec item patch @nonexistent --data '{...}' runs
   425→            then: 'error: Item not found: @nonexistent'
