   797→        title: Commit Message Guidance
   798→        type: feature
   799→        tags:
   800→          - process
   801→          - traceability
   802→        description: >-
   803→          Outputs suggested commit messages with standardized trailers after completing tasks or
   804→          during session checkpoint. Reinforces trailer convention for traceability and enables
   805→          kspec log searches.
   806→
   807→
   808→          Trailer format:
   809→
   810→          - Task: @task-slug (always present)
   811→
   812→          - Spec: @spec-ref (if task.spec_ref exists)
   813→
   814→
   815→          When no spec_ref: prompts agent to consider if spec coverage is needed.
   816→
   817→
   818→          Output triggers:
   819→
   820→          - task complete: Full commit message suggestion
   821→
   822→          - session checkpoint: WIP commit guidance when task in_progress with uncommitted changes
   823→        depends_on: []
   824→        implements: []
   825→        relates_to: []
   826→        tests: []
   827→        created: '2026-01-16T18:42:37.515Z'
   828→        acceptance_criteria:
   829→          - id: ac-1
   830→            given: task has spec_ref
   831→            when: task complete runs
   832→            then: 'output includes both Task: and Spec: trailers'
   833→          - id: ac-2
   834→            given: task has no spec_ref
   835→            when: task complete runs
   836→            then: 'output includes Task: trailer and warning about potential spec gap'
   837→          - id: ac-3
   838→            given: task in_progress with uncommitted changes
   839→            when: session checkpoint runs
   840→            then: WIP commit guidance included in instructions
   841→          - id: ac-4
   842→            given: JSON mode enabled
   843→            when: commit guidance would be shown
   844→            then: guidance is suppressed (JSON output only)
