  1180→    slugs:
  1181→      - derive-commands
  1182→    title: Derive Commands
  1183→    type: feature
  1184→    status:
  1185→      maturity: draft
  1186→      implementation: not_started
  1187→    priority: high
  1188→    tags:
  1189→      - mvp
  1190→      - cli
  1191→    description: |
  1192→      Commands for deriving tasks from spec items.
  1193→      Explicit, on-demand task creation.
  1194→    requirements:
  1195→      - _ulid: 01JHNKAA06CDRV100000000000
  1196→        slugs:
  1197→          - cmd-derive
  1198→        title: kspec derive
  1199→        type: requirement
  1200→        status:
  1201→          maturity: draft
  1202→          implementation: implemented
  1203→        description: |
  1204→          kspec derive <ref> [options]
  1205→          kspec derive --all [options]
  1206→
  1207→          Derives implementation tasks from spec items.
  1208→
  1209→          Behavior:
  1210→          - Recursively creates tasks for item and all children
  1211→          - Features create feature tasks
  1212→          - Requirements create requirement tasks under feature
  1213→          - Auto-sets depends_on based on spec hierarchy:
  1214→            - Requirement tasks depend on parent feature task
  1215→            - Child features depend on parent module task
  1216→          - Skips items that already have tasks (unless --force)
  1217→
  1218→          Options:
  1219→          - --recursive: Derive for item and all children (default)
  1220→          - --flat: Only derive for the specified item, no children
  1221→          - --force: Create even if task exists
  1222→          - --dry-run: Show what would be created
  1223→          - --json: Output created tasks as JSON
  1224→
  1225→          Examples:
  1226→            kspec derive @shadow-branch
  1227→            # Creates tasks for module + all features + all requirements
  1228→            # with proper depends_on relationships
  1229→
  1230→            kspec derive @shadow-concept --flat
  1231→            # Creates single task for just that feature
  1232→
  1233→          Idempotent by default.
  1234→        implements:
  1235→          - '@derive-commands'
  1236→          - '@derive-command'
  1237→        acceptance_criteria:
  1238→          - id: ac-1
  1239→            given: a spec item with no children
  1240→            when: kspec derive @item runs
  1241→            then: 'creates one task with spec_ref=@item; outputs ''Created task: <ref>'''
  1242→          - id: ac-2
  1243→            given: a module with 2 child features
  1244→            when: kspec derive @module runs
  1245→            then: creates 3 tasks (module + 2 features); each task has correct spec_ref
  1246→          - id: ac-3
  1247→            given: a module with child features
  1248→            when: kspec derive @module --flat runs
  1249→            then: creates 1 task for module only; children are not processed
  1250→          - id: ac-4
  1251→            given: a feature under a module
  1252→            when: derive creates tasks for both
  1253→            then: feature task has depends_on containing module task ref
  1254→          - id: ac-5
  1255→            given: a requirement under a feature
  1256→            when: derive creates tasks for both
  1257→            then: requirement task has depends_on containing feature task ref
  1258→          - id: ac-6
  1259→            given: module task already exists, feature has no task
  1260→            when: kspec derive @feature runs
  1261→            then: feature task depends_on references existing module task
  1262→          - id: ac-7
  1263→            given: a spec item already has a linked task
  1264→            when: kspec derive @item runs (no --force)
  1265→            then: 'no task created; outputs ''Skipped @item (task exists: @task-ref)'''
  1266→          - id: ac-8
  1267→            given: module has task, feature-a has task, feature-b has no task
  1268→            when: kspec derive @module runs
  1269→            then: only feature-b task created; module and feature-a skipped with message
  1270→          - id: ac-9
  1271→            given: a spec item already has a linked task
  1272→            when: kspec derive @item --force runs
  1273→            then: new task created; outputs warning 'Created duplicate task for @item'
  1274→          - id: ac-10
  1275→            given: a module with children
  1276→            when: kspec derive @module --dry-run runs
  1277→            then: outputs 'Would create:' followed by task list; no tasks actually created; exit 0
  1278→          - id: ac-11
  1279→            given: derive creates tasks
  1280→            when: '--json flag is passed'
  1281→            then: >-
  1282→              outputs JSON array with objects {ulid, slug, spec_ref, depends_on, action:
  1283→              'created'|'skipped'}
  1284→          - id: ac-12
  1285→            given: 3 spec items exist, 1 already has a task
  1286→            when: kspec derive --all runs
  1287→            then: creates tasks for 2 items without tasks; skips the one with existing task
  1288→          - id: ac-13
  1289→            given: '@nonexistent does not resolve'
  1290→            when: kspec derive @nonexistent runs
  1291→            then: 'exits code 1; error ''Reference not found: @nonexistent'''
  1292→          - id: ac-14
  1293→            given: all spec items already have tasks
  1294→            when: kspec derive --all runs
  1295→            then: outputs 'Nothing to derive (all items have tasks)'; exit 0
