  1352→        slugs:
  1353→          - cmd-setup
  1354→        title: kspec setup
  1355→        type: requirement
  1356→        tags:
  1357→          - mvp
  1358→          - cli
  1359→        description: >-
  1360→          kspec setup [options]
  1361→
  1362→
  1363→          Configures agent environment for kspec. Auto-detects the running agent and installs
  1364→          appropriate configuration.
  1365→
  1366→
  1367→          Agent Detection:
  1368→
  1369→          - claude-code (via CLAUDECODE, CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT, etc.)
  1370→
  1371→          - aider (via AIDER_* env vars)
  1372→
  1373→          - cline/roo-code (VS Code extensions)
  1374→
  1375→          - copilot-cli, gemini-cli, codex-cli, opencode, amp
  1376→
  1377→
  1378→          Actions:
  1379→
  1380→          - Sets KSPEC_AUTHOR in agent config file (e.g., ~/.claude/settings.json)
  1381→
  1382→          - For Claude Code: installs hooks to .claude/settings.json (project-level):
  1383→            - UserPromptSubmit: spec-first reminder (session prompt-check)
  1384→            - Stop: session checkpoint for uncommitted work
  1385→          - Prints manual instructions for agents without config file support
  1386→
  1387→
  1388→          Options:
  1389→
  1390→          - --dry-run: Show what would be done without making changes
  1391→
  1392→          - --author <author>: Custom author string (default: auto-detected like @claude, @aider)
  1393→
  1394→          - --no-hooks: Skip installing Claude Code hooks
  1395→
  1396→          - --force: Overwrite existing configuration
  1397→
  1398→
  1399→          Exit codes follow @cli-exit-codes.
