  1562→    title: Fuzzy Matching
  1563→    type: feature
  1564→    priority: medium
  1565→    tags:
  1566→      - dx
  1567→      - cli
  1568→    description: >-
  1569→      Infrastructure for fuzzy string matching across kspec. Enables approximate matching for
  1570→      item/task search and CLI command suggestions. Uses Levenshtein distance or similar algorithm
  1571→      for scoring matches.
  1572→    depends_on: []
  1573→    implements: []
  1574→    relates_to: []
  1575→    tests: []
  1576→    created: '2026-01-15T17:11:48.677Z'
  1577→    requirements:
  1578→      - _ulid: 01KF1A8Z6VHV4TKGS9GNZHSDZA
  1579→        slugs:
  1580→          - fuzzy-item-search
  1581→        title: Grep-like Content Search
  1582→        type: requirement
  1583→        tags:
  1584→          - dx
  1585→          - search
  1586→        description: >-
  1587→          kspec search <pattern>
  1588→
  1589→          kspec item list --grep <pattern>
  1590→
  1591→          kspec tasks list --grep <pattern>
  1592→
  1593→
  1594→          Enables content search across all spec items and tasks. Searches ALL text content
  1595→          including titles, descriptions, notes, and acceptance criteria text.
  1596→
  1597→
  1598→          Behavior:
  1599→
  1600→          - Pattern is treated as regex (like grep)
  1601→
  1602→          - Case-insensitive by default
  1603→
  1604→          - Searches recursively through all text fields
  1605→
  1606→          - Returns the ITEMS/TASKS themselves (not line snippets)
  1607→
  1608→          - Shows which field(s) matched for context
  1609→
  1610→          - Works with existing filters (--type, --tag, etc.)
  1611→
  1612→
  1613→          Examples:
  1614→
  1615→          - kspec search "TODO" → returns all items/tasks mentioning TODO
  1616→
  1617→          - kspec search "shadow.*branch" → regex pattern across all content
  1618→
  1619→          - kspec tasks list --grep "authentication" → tasks mentioning authentication
  1620→
  1621→
  1622→          Output shows items with match location:
  1623→
  1624→          01KF1234 [pending] P2 Implement auth flow
  1625→            matched: notes[1].content, description
  1626→
  1627→          The search finds items; the pattern is just the filter criteria.
  1628→        depends_on: []
  1629→        implements: []
  1630→        relates_to: []
  1631→        tests: []
  1632→        created: '2026-01-15T17:11:58.428Z'
  1633→        status:
  1634→          maturity: draft
  1635→          implementation: implemented
  1636→        acceptance_criteria:
  1637→          - id: ac-1
  1638→            given: A user runs kspec search "TODO"
  1639→            when: The search runs across all loaded items and tasks
  1640→            then: >-
  1641→              Returns items/tasks where any text field matches, showing the item itself (not just
  1642→              the matched line)
  1643→          - id: ac-2
  1644→            given: A user searches with a regex pattern like "shadow.*branch"
  1645→            when: The pattern is applied to content
  1646→            then: Matches using JavaScript regex semantics, case-insensitive by default
  1647→          - id: ac-3
  1648→            given: An item matches in multiple fields
  1649→            when: Results are displayed
  1650→            then: >-
  1651→              Shows which field(s) matched (e.g., matched: notes[1].content, description) for
  1652→              context
  1653→          - id: ac-4
  1654→            given: A match is found in nested content like notes or AC
  1655→            when: Results are displayed
  1656→            then: >-
  1657→              The full item is returned with match location indicator, not just the matched text
  1658→              snippet
  1659→          - id: ac-5
  1660→            given: User combines search with filters like --type task or --status pending
  1661→            when: Search runs
  1662→            then: Filters are applied first, then content search within the filtered set
  1663→          - id: ac-6
  1664→            given: Search finds no matches
  1665→            when: Results are displayed
  1666→            then: Shows empty result with helpful message, not an error
  1667→      - _ulid: 01KF1A991VFFQ99EBQGQ9XB55D
  1668→        slugs:
  1669→          - fuzzy-command-suggest
  1670→        title: CLI Command Suggestions on Error
  1671→        type: requirement
  1672→        tags:
  1673→          - dx
  1674→          - cli
  1675→          - errors
  1676→        description: |-
  1677→          When user enters an invalid command, suggest close matches.
  1678→
  1679→          Behavior:
  1680→          - On unknown command, compute distance to all valid commands
  1681→          - If close match found (e.g., 'task list' vs 'tasks list'), suggest it
  1682→          - Threshold-based: only suggest if match is close enough
  1683→          - Also handles subcommand typos (e.g., 'inbox ad' → 'inbox add')
  1684→
  1685→          Output format:
  1686→            error: Unknown command 'task list'
  1687→            Did you mean: kspec tasks list?
  1688→
  1689→          Consider also accepting common aliases:
  1690→          - 'task' as alias for 'tasks' (singular/plural flexibility)
  1691→          - 'ls' as alias for 'list'
  1692→          - Other common patterns from git/npm conventions
