  1827→        slugs:
  1828→          - ralph-output-formatting
  1829→        title: Ralph Output Formatting
  1830→        type: requirement
  1831→        tags: []
  1832→        description: >-
  1833→          Structured formatting for ralph streaming output. Translates ACP events into readable CLI
  1834→          output with visual separation between agent messages, tool calls, and results. Follows
  1835→          patterns from kynetic chat/session UI with chalk-based colors, section headers,
  1836→          timestamps, and noise suppression.
  1837→
  1838→
  1839→          Key learnings from kynetic beads history:
  1840→
  1841→          - Finalization is critical for streaming state
  1842→
  1843→          - Library limitations guide input format requirements
  1844→
  1845→          - Tests must verify end-to-end rendered output
  1846→
  1847→          - Treat LLM output as untrusted content
  1848→
  1849→
  1850→          Implementation references:
  1851→
  1852→          - ui-event-translator.ts pattern for ACP event translation
  1853→
  1854→          - event-display.ts for display summaries
  1855→
  1856→          - aggregated-message.ts for message structure
  1857→        depends_on: []
  1858→        implements: []
  1859→        relates_to: []
  1860→        tests: []
  1861→        created: '2026-01-17T19:01:42.519Z'
  1862→        acceptance_criteria:
  1863→          - id: ac-1
  1864→            given: ACP agent streams agent_message events
  1865→            when: messages are displayed in CLI
  1866→            then: >-
  1867→              messages show with visual separation (section header or newline), chalk.blue for
  1868→              content, and streaming indicator while incomplete
  1869→          - id: ac-2
  1870→            given: ACP agent streams tool_call and tool_call_update events
  1871→            when: tool calls are displayed in CLI
  1872→            then: >-
  1873→              shows tool name, input summary (command for Bash, path for Read/Write, pattern for
  1874→              Grep/Glob), status indicator (pending/running/completed/failed), and truncated output
  1875→              (first 20 lines or 1000 chars with expansion hint)
  1876→          - id: ac-3
  1877→            given: ralph is streaming output
  1878→            when: each significant event is displayed
  1879→            then: >-
  1880→              shows relative timestamp from session start (e.g., +5s, +2m) prefixed to the event
  1881→              line
  1882→          - id: ac-4
  1883→            given: ACP agent emits debug or internal log messages (e.g., 'No onPostToolUseHook found')
  1884→            when: these messages arrive in the event stream
  1885→            then: messages are suppressed from CLI output (logged to session events only)
  1886→          - id: ac-5
  1887→            given: message stream ends (empty chunk or status event)
  1888→            when: finalization signal is received
  1889→            then: current streaming message is marked complete and any pending formatting is applied
  1890→        status:
  1891→          maturity: draft
  1892→          implementation: implemented
