  2026→    slugs:
  2027→      - cmd-session-checkpoint
  2028→    title: kspec session checkpoint
  2029→    type: requirement
  2030→    tags: []
  2031→    description: >-
  2032→      Pre-stop hook for Claude Code integration.
  2033→
  2034→
  2035→      Checks for uncommitted work before allowing session to end:
  2036→
  2037→      - Uncommitted git changes (staged, unstaged, untracked)
  2038→
  2039→      - Tasks in in_progress status
  2040→
  2041→      - Incomplete todos on active tasks
  2042→
  2043→
  2044→      One-time trigger: Reads stop_hook_active from Claude Code stdin JSON to detect retry. First
  2045→      trigger blocks with instructions, subsequent triggers allow stop.
  2046→
  2047→
  2048→      Output: JSON formatted for Claude Code hook consumption with clear kspec-branded message
  2049→      instructing agent to document progress and commit changes. Uses {"decision": "block",
  2050→      "reason": "..."} format.
  2051→
  2052→
  2053→      Installation: kspec setup automatically installs this hook to project-level
  2054→      .claude/settings.json for Claude Code users. Hook format requires matcher field (even if empty
  2055→      string).
  2056→
  2057→
  2058→      Acceptance Criteria:
  2059→
  2060→      - AC1: Instructions are numbered sequentially based on which issues apply (dynamic numbering,
  2061→      not hardcoded)
  2062→
  2063→      - AC2: Only relevant instructions shown (e.g., if no in_progress tasks, those steps are
  2064→      omitted)
  2065→
  2066→      - AC3: Exit silently with no output when session can end cleanly
