  2082→        description: >-
  2083→          UserPromptSubmit hook for spec-first workflow reinforcement.
  2084→
  2085→
  2086→          Outputs a lean reminder on every user prompt: '[kspec] Before implementing behavior
  2087→          changes, check spec coverage. Update spec first if needed.'
  2088→
  2089→
  2090→          Design rationale:
  2091→
  2092→          - Always injects (no filtering) - Claude is smart enough to apply when relevant
  2093→
  2094→          - Minimal token overhead - short, instructive message
  2095→
  2096→          - Non-blocking - context injection, not gating
  2097→
  2098→
  2099→          Installation: kspec setup automatically installs this hook alongside session checkpoint to
  2100→          project-level .claude/settings.json for Claude Code users.
  2101→
  2102→
  2103→          Acceptance Criteria:
  2104→
  2105→          - AC1: Outputs single-line reminder to stdout
  2106→
  2107→          - AC2: No stdin parsing required (stateless)
  2108→
  2109→          - AC3: Installed by setup command as UserPromptSubmit hook
